{"name":"Tanning gummies / supplements","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":109,"casual":{"lead":["Tanning gummies and pills are taken by mouth to give skin a deeper, golden look from the inside. They typically contain carotenoids such as beta-carotene.","Carotenoids deposit in body fat and skin and tint it. Older tanning pills used canthaxanthin, which was known to give a golden-orange colour. The US FDA has said no tanning pills are approved and has sent warning letters to sellers, and no trial of a tan-boost chew for appearance has been located."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["People take them daily as a supplement, often alongside sun exposure or self-tan, and report colour building gradually over weeks."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["High-dose canthaxanthin has been linked to retinal deposits, liver injury and hives, and the FDA treats such products as adulterated cosmetics with an unsafe colour additive. Beta-carotene at high doses has been linked to lung cancer in smokers, and the American Cancer Society notes it is not approved for tanning."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"Calcium, vitamin D, or combined supplementation to prevent fractures and falls: systematic review and meta-analysis.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/42161415/","source":"BMJ (Clinical research ed.)","year":2026,"cites":null,"kind":"Systematic Review"},{"title":"Effects of Collagen Supplements on Skin Aging: A Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis of Randomized Controlled Trials.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40324552/","source":"The American journal of medicine","year":2025,"cites":null,"kind":"Systematic Review"},{"title":"Effect of collagen supplementation on knee osteoarthritis: an updated systematic review and meta-analysis of randomised controlled trials.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39212129/","source":"Clinical and experimental rheumatology","year":2025,"cites":null,"kind":"Meta-Analysis"},{"tit