Fish oil supplements linked to prostate cancer (2013)","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=19471547","site":"Hacker News","score":111,"comments":65,"year":2019},{"title":"Taking dietary supplements full of antioxidants could help cancerous tumors grow","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=37349870","site":"Hacker News","score":107,"comments":66,"year":2023},{"title":"Amphetamines Are Hiding in Your Supplements","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=9345340","site":"Hacker News","score":99,"comments":72,"year":2015},{"title":"Vitamin D supplements cut heart attack risk by 52%. Why?","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46830667","site":"Hacker News","score":104,"comments":50,"year":2026},{"title":"Show HN: Find out where your supplements are made & sourced","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=32029625","site":"Hacker News","score":109,"comments":37,"year":2022}],"web":[{"title":"Tanning (leather) — Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tanning_(leather)"},{"title":"Sunless tanning (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunless_tanning"},{"title":"Canthaxanthin (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canthaxanthin"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Tan & skin tone","chain":["Carotenoid taken orally","Pigment deposits in skin and fat","Golden, deeper-looking skin"],"effect":"indirect","text":"Tanning gummies and pills use carotenoids such as beta-carotene that deposit in skin and body fat, aiming for a golden, deeper-looking tone. Older canthaxanthin pills gave a golden-orange tint; no tanning pill is FDA-approved."},"wikipedia":{"title":"Tanning (leather)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tanning_(leather)"},"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Tanning gummies and supplements are oral products marketed to boost or deepen a tan, typically containing carotenoids such as beta-carotene. A related older category, tanning pills, used canthaxanthin, a carotenoid that deposits in body fat and gives a golden-orange tint.[1][2]","The US FDA has said no tanning pills are approved and has sent warning letters to sellers, calling such products adulterated cosmetics because they contain an unsafe colour additive.[2] The American Cancer Society states beta-carotene is not FDA-approved for tanning.[1] No clinical trial of a tan-boost chew for appearance has been located."],"infobox":[["Type","Oral supplement / pill"],["Typical ingredients","Beta-carotene, canthaxanthin"],["Approval for tanning","None (US)"]],"sections":[{"h":"Canthaxanthin","paras":["Canthaxanthin is permitted as a food and feed colour, but not as a tanning agent. In the late 1980s reversible crystal deposits in the retina were reported in some people taking very high doses from tanning pills, and the FDA links such pills to canthaxanthin retinopathy, reported liver injury and hives.[2] A 2011 study reported no lasting structural changes.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Beta-carotene","paras":["High synthetic doses of beta-carotene have been linked to higher lung cancer rates among smokers.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1980s","event":"Retinal crystal deposits reported with high-dose canthaxanthin tanning pills.[2]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Sunless tanning","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunless_tanning","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Canthaxanthin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canthaxanthin","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Supplements","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/supplements.1822937/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260208173727/https://looksmax.org/threads/supplements.1822937/"},{"title":"Supplements - Cope or Dope?","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/supplements-cope-or-dope.1813052/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260215014950/https://looksmax.org/threads/supplements-co